<Base title="ConsDRED"><main class="wrap feature-index"><div class="feature-index-intro"><span>RESEARCH / IEEE TASE 2025</span><h1>ConsDRED</h1><p>Constrained reinforcement learning using distributional representation for trustworthy quadrotor UAV tracking control.</p></div><div class="feature-consdred-detail"><img src="/research/consdred-demo-still.jpg" alt="ConsDRED demonstration showing real-world quadrotor flight and simulation views"/><div><h2>Tracking under uncertainty</h2><p>ConsDRED combines a distributional reinforcement-learning disturbance estimator with stochastic model predictive control, addressing uncertain aerodynamic effects and constrained trajectory tracking.</p><p>Yanran Wang and David Boyle · IEEE Transactions on Automation Science and Engineering, volume 22, pages 5877–5894 (2025). Also presented at IROS 2025.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TASE.2024.3432405">DOI / Paper ↗</a><a href="https://alex-yanranwang.github.io/ConsDRED-SMPC.html">Project ↗</a><a href="/research/">Research index ↗</a></div></div></div><figure class="feature-consdred-secondary"><img src="/research/consdred-trajectory.png" alt="ConsDRED reference trajectory and external disturbance zones"/><figcaption>Trajectory and disturbance-zone illustration, Wang &amp; Boyle, IEEE TASE 2025.</figcaption></figure></main></Base>
